      "receiptId": "sparrow-dumpling.html-1",
      "receiptSource": "Original Receipt in \u0027\u003Ci\u003EThe Experienced English Housekeeper\u003C/i\u003E\u0027 by Elizabeth Raffald (\u003Ca href=\u0022references.html#raffald-1769\u0022\u003E\u003Cb\u003ERaffald 1769\u003C/b\u003E\u003C/a\u003E)",
      "receiptText": "\u003Cb\u003ETO MAKE A SPARROW DUMPLING\u003C/b\u003E\u003Cbr\u003E\nMix half a Pint of good Milk with three Eggs, a little Salt, and as much Flour as will make it a thick Batter, put a Lump of Butter rolled in Pepper and Salt in every Sparrow, mix them in the Batter, and tie them in a Cloth, boil them one Hour and a half, pour melted Butter over them, and serve it up\u003Cbr\u003E"
